# Protected inline boundary: pin only the verified protected-neutral attribute subset.
# Checked by tests/architecture/inline_boundary_test.rs; extending it requires pre-LTO body, inline-tree
# and level-3 callee-contract comparisons, followed by the lead's fat-build A/B.
#
# Columns (TAB separated): kind, file (relative to crates/neovm-core/src), item, reach, # reason
#   kind   always  inlined into a protected function in the reference build: #[inline(always)]
#          never   called out of line from a protected function: #[inline(never)]
#          exempt  reached, but not pinnable without re-tuning other call sites, or
#                  without code at the protected site (see the reason); must still exist as a fn
#          generated  a specifically identified macro invocation must generate the item
#   item   name | Type::name | <Type as Trait>::name, spelled as in the enclosing impl header
#   reach  protected functions that reach it; `root` marks a protected function itself, `inline`
#          independently retains body scanning even when its hint is exempt
#
# Derived 2026-10-06 from the DWARF inline tree and call targets of the reference fat-LTO build
# tmp/v10x/b37cand-bin/neomacs (main 3a3ffdfb1c, build-wt.sh: profiling profile, CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0).
# Not listed: compiler-generated code (derives, closures, drop glue, std/thread-local internals);
# the binary guard tmp/v10x/protected-codegen-check.sh pins those through the inline tree.
# When the guard's table is re-pinned for an intended change, re-derive this list from the same build.

